      "rationale": "🫥️ RECLASSIFIED. The third-party crate here does REAL codec work — it decodes the artifact and will reject a malformed one — but that is not what the mutation test turns on. What the OUTPUT OF A MUTATION SHOULD BE is computed by this owner's own `🧪️oracle/🦀️component.rs`, whose `apply_kind` dispatch is a second implementation of this subset's mutation semantics. Its own doc comment says so: it \"deliberately mirrors\" the production `diff` rather than diverging from it. Both halves of the comparison therefore read the same specification, and a misreading of it produces two agreeing wrong answers.\n\nThe honest split is that the crate discharges \"the result is a well-formed file of this format\", and NOT \"the mutation computed the right answer\". Only the second is what a mutation oracle is for, so this is a `cross-semio-implementation`: a required SUPPLEMENT, never a substitute. A qualifying third-party reference for the mutation semantics is still owed.",
